      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Hi,</p><p>I guess it is possible, just make sure that each of your debug configurations has a unique server port and the correct serial number.</p><p>Best regards,</p><p>Elliot</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>​<user-mention data-id=\"107916\">@beru</user-mention> </p><p>STM32CubeIDE Eclipse and STM32CubeIDE for VS Code can coexist without issues.</p><p>STM32CubeIDE for VS Code provides a feature that converts Eclipse projects to CMake. CMake project(s) are supported by both IDEs.</p><p> </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/305c144a-2eea-4529-957d-88d38fda5b28.png\"/></figure><p> </p></div>"
